  "disambiguation_summary": "vary-parse is distinct from every shipped parser: vs. etagparse the wildcard * means 'do not cache locally' (not entity-tag-match); vs. cache-control-parse there is no '=' syntax and no closed directive vocabulary; vs. sfvparse Vary is intentionally NOT a Structured Field (RFC 8941 \u00a71.3 compatibility-listed). vary-parse is the only header parser in the family that implements the wildcard semantics and the cache-key construction helper."
